content='```yaml\n---\n- name: Check if Helm binary exists\n  stat:\n    path: "{{ helm_binary_path }}"\n  register: helm_binary\n\n- name: Check Helm version\n  command: "{{ helm_binary_path }} version --short"\n  register: helm_version\n  when: helm_binary.stat.exists\n\n- name: Download helm\n  get_url:\n    url: "{{ helm_download_url }}"\n    dest: "/tmp/helm.tar.gz"\n  when: not helm_binary.stat.exists or helm_version.stdout is version(helm_required_version, "<")\n\n- name: Copy helm binary into place\n  copy:\n    src: "/tmp/helm.tar.gz"\n    dest: "{{ helm_binary_path }}"\n    mode: \'0755\'\n  when: not helm_binary.stat.exists or helm_version.stdout is version(helm_required_version, "<")\n```\n\nThis playbook is structured to be included in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/` directory, such as `tasks/main.yml`. It follows the exact task names and module calls as specified, ensuring compliance with the requirements.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T21:02:28.384813228Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 2986011879, 'load_duration': 41802303, 'prompt_eval_count': 362, 'prompt_eval_duration': 35123644, 'eval_count': 218, 'eval_duration': 2908394824, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--b9264af6-7e41-4091-9bdf-cb2f3d1b4394-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 362, 'output_tokens': 218, 'total_tokens': 580}
